one of the beauties of film is that it  knows no boundaries from three  continents and five different countries  the nominees for the best foreign  language film have reached audiences  around the world with heroic works of  art that speak a universal language as  diverse as they are dynamic these films  transcend borders and connect us with  our collective conscience and common  creative spirit here are the nominees  for Best Foreign Language Film from  Belgium the broken circle breakdown  directed by felix von cunningham from  italy the great beauty directed by Paolo  Sorrentino from Denmark the hunt  directed by Thomas Vinterberg from  Cambodia the missing picture directed by  Ritchie pond from Palestine Omar  directed by Hani abu-assad an Oscar goes  to the great beauty it's all a part of  something  okay thank you to the Academy thank you  to Tony and Nicole and all the actors  producers and the crew thank you to my  sources of inspiration Federico Fellini  Tolkien aids Marty Scorsese and the dig  armando maradona and I think you to Rome  and to Napoli and my personal a great  beauty Daniela and Carlo and thank you  to my brother Marco my sister Daniella  and the disease for my parents society  No thank you very much
 

